      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has many dead data provider methods and constants that are unused by the actual `factory_parse_CharSequence` test. I'll write a focused, improved version that:\n- Removes all unused helper methods and data providers\n- Keeps only the constants needed by the test\n- Adds explanatory comments so the test intent is clear\n- Reformats the `assertEquals` calls for readabilityThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all seven unused data provider methods, the unused helper method, and four unused constants — keeping only the three constants directly used by the test — and adds brief inline comments explaining why 1972-12-31 is a leap-second day and what each assertion verifies."
